I moved yoyo to yoagent 0.27.7 and deleted the hand-kept Gemini limits table. Every Gemini id yoyo offers now gets its limits from yoagent's presets. It's committed as f91dcacc with both Fixes #1168 and Fixes #1164. Build, the full test suite (6889 passed, 0 failed), clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check are all green.

What changed:
• The bump on its own turned exactly the two guards built to fail red, by name, before I deleted anything: every_offered_gemini_id_has_a_preset_or_a_published_limits_row and every_offered_gemini_id_is_a_yoagent_preset_or_on_googles_page.
• Deleted GOOGLE_PUBLISHED_LIMITS, google_published_limits, google_limits_beyond_preset and their three readers: the Google run path, the #943 output ceiling and /model info. Those now read only ModelConfig::preset("google", id). The grep for the three names is empty in src/, docs/ and README.md.
• Guards turned around, no tests deleted. Both guards now check that every offered or picker Gemini id has a yoagent preset whose window and output differ from the generic 1,000,000 / 8192 guess. I renamed them for that. The run-path test now covers every offered id's preset, and still pins flash-lite at 1,048,576 / 65,536.
• New `/cost` test: flash_lite_has_a_bundled_price checks that flash-lite is priced through yoagent's row.
• Positive controls: for each mutation I counted the NEUTERED marker before running, broke the check, watched it fail by name, then restored it and saw it pass. That covered both guards and the price test. No markers are left in the tree.

One thing the full run found that the task didn't predict: a price-audit test went red. /cost now bills flash-lite from yoagent's new price row, which reads a $0 cache-write rate as "bill at the input rate" ($0.10). The test expected models.dev's $0. This follows @yuanhao's #1012 decision that yoyo reuses yoagent's prices. It costs users nothing, because yoagent's Google provider only ever fills in cache reads, so no cache-write tokens are billed. I made that test read its expected value from yoagent's table, the same way its OpenAI neighbour already does.

Other notes:
• cargo update also changed some unrelated windows-sys pins in Cargo.lock. I cut the lock diff back to yoagent's version and checksum only, and cargo build --locked accepts it.
• I updated the size register for agent_builder.rs (4997 lines) and commands_info.rs (3559). Both files shrank, but the register had been behind HEAD.
• docs/src/configuration/models.md no longer says flash-lite lacks a yoagent preset. ARCHITECTURE.md quotes the old table's reason and marks it superseded, dated Day 254.
• Left alone: yoyo's own price rule for names containing gemini-2.5-flash-lite in format/cost.rs. It no longer answers for the exact id, but still covers longer variant names. The commit says so.
